{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-41918","model_call":22,"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ plutonium (+ radioisotope thermoelectric generators rtg rtgs) (+ reliable continuous long-lived))"},"record":{"query":{"op":"query","query":"(^ plutonium (+ radioisotope thermoelectric generators rtg rtgs) (+ reliable continuous long-lived))"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_22_944649975#8_2118930959","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q970","rank":1,"snippet":"238 made? What is INL’s role? Who is funding the production of Pu-238? Multimedia Gallery MARS 2020 ROVER by Marco_Romero \" , \"segment\": \"The system has a design life of 17 years, but can be expected to produce power much longer than that. Additionally, the MMRTG provides a source of heat for the rover’s instruments and on-board systems in the cold environment. Thermocouples have no moving parts and have proved an amazingly <cover>reliable source of energy for space missions. More Info TIMELINE This timeline provides information on each milestone for the Mars 2020 Multi-Mission Radioisotope Thermoelectric Generator. Scroll through the timeline events below. HOT TOPICS National labs resume plutonium </cover>production for space exploration While the United States has enough plutonium to fuel the space missions scheduled for the next decade, the domestic supply of plutonium is a limited resource. In order to establish a new supply of Pu-238 to enable future NASA missions, Congress directed the Department of Energy (DOE) to resume Pu-238 production. Read More To Pluto and beyond: Work that reaches the stars They’ve stayed in the same spot for more than a decade, but ","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_22_944649975#8_2118930959","rank":1,"relevance":3}]},"time":211},"model_calls":22,"document_judgments":19,"relevance_3":14,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
