{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-41918","model_call":42,"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ plutonium (+ \"what is plutonium used for\" uses applications) (+ spacecraft pacemakers reactors))"},"record":{"query":{"op":"query","query":"(^ plutonium (+ \"what is plutonium used for\" uses applications) (+ spacecraft pacemakers reactors))"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_08_1256106727#13_2266413751","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q980","rank":1,"snippet":"ELIMINATING URANIUM AND PLUTONIUM? “Thorium is considered by some as the nuclear fuel of the future.” INDIA LEADS THE WAY THORIUM – REACHING AROUND THE WORLD “After India, the main countries driving thorium research are America and Russia.” WHEN WILL THORIUM MAKE AN IMPRESSION? THE FUTURE FOR THORIUM \" , \"segment\": \"India has a three-stage plan for nuclear energy. Stage one uses uranium-fuelled PHWRs (pressurised heavy water reactors) and LWRs to produce plutonium. In stage two this plutonium-based fuel is used in FBRs to breed U-233, and more <cover>plutonium and thorium. Stage three uses advanced heavy water reactors </cover>to burn the U-233 and Pu-239 with thorium. The thorium will produce around 75% of the power, with the spent fuel being reprocessed to recycle fissile materials. “Thorium is a much safer fuel source than uranium or plutonium.” India views ADS as a definite contender for power in the near term and for incinerating long-lived radioactive waste from the uranium fuel cycle. It has been studying all aspects of the ADS subsystems and work is continuing on improvements to beam current from the driver accelerator and improve thermal hydraulics and materials compatibility. ","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_08_1256106727#13_2266413751","rank":1,"relevance":1}]},"time":7851},"model_calls":42,"document_judgments":38,"relevance_3":21,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
