{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-41918","model_call":44,"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q980"},"record":{"query":{"op":"next","qid":"q980"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_18_1152658657#0_1303710121","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q980","rank":5,"snippet":"{ \"docid\": \"msmarco_v2.1_doc_18_1152658657#0_1303710121\" , \"end_char\": 1904.000000 , \"headings\": \"Plutonium-238 Plutonium-238 Contents History Initial production Human radiation experiments Weapons Use in radioisotope thermoelectric generators Nuclear powered <cover>pacemakers Production U.S. production ceases and resumes Applications See also References External links \" , \"segment\": \"Plutonium-</cover>238 - Wikipedia Plutonium-238 From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia Jump to navigation Jump to search Isotope of plutonium used in radioisotope thermoelectric generators Plutonium-238, 238 Pu Plutonium-238 oxide pellet glowing from its self-heating General Symbol 238 Pu Names plutonium-238, Pu-238 Protons 94 Neutrons 144 Nuclide data Half-life 87.7 years Parent isotopes 242 Cm ( α) 238 Np ( β −) 238 Am ( β +) Decay products 234 U Isotope mass 238.049553 u Spin 0 Decay modes Decay mode Decay energy ( MeV) Alpha decay 5.593 Isotopes of plutonium Complete table of nuclides Plutonium-238 ( 238 Pu) is a radioactive isotope of plutonium that has a half-life of 87.7 years. Plutonium-238 is a very powerful alpha emitter; as alpha particles are easily ","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_18_1152658657#0_1303710121","rank":5,"relevance":3}]},"time":16},"model_calls":44,"document_judgments":40,"relevance_3":23,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
